@title A jump from the outline glides to its target (motion on)
@area Schematic
@sizes 1920x1080
@env KOPERCAD_MOTION=1
# Polish: a jump (outline row, problem, cross reference) glides for 220 ms instead of cutting. The harness normally runs without ambient motion (KOPERCAD_MOTION unset), so this scenario turns it on. The page starts fitted; the jump zooms in on wire 1 and, after the glide, it sits at the centre of the drawing. Only the end state is a stable picture; the glide itself is covered by a canvas unit test (the jump starts where the view was and lands on time, any drag or wheel stops it).
click_text "Open example"
wait 20
click_text "Drawn wires"
wait 6
click_text "Page 1 (17)"
wait 6
shot page-fitted
click 120 592
wait_s 1
shot after-the-jump
check_layout
